  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Deep Maw Krixizak
    
    An orca raider of the Still Pools shallows, known principally — and only — through the partnership with **Krathund Gnurl**, the scarred pod-mate whose name translates roughly as *the-one-who-takes*. The two were the last surviving pair of their pod, a fact neither the oral accounts nor the ice-impressions trouble to explain. Pods do not reduce to two members through ordinary attrition. Something happened before the record begins, and no source I have found addresses it.
    
    Maw's dorsal fin carries a pressure-lance notch from the Orca Incursion — healed wrong, permanently visible. The same engagement left Maw deaf on the left side. The summary attributes this wound to one 'Otrolal; the chronicle account names no assailant. I have not located 'Otrolal in any other record. The deafness was functional, not total: deep-songs registered only as vibration through the jawbone, while the right ear compensated. Maw wore penguin beaks on a kelp-cord and counted them in whispers. The ritual predated the dead god's silence and apparently outlasted it, though by then it had become rote.
    
    What the accounts emphasize is position. Maw held Krath's left flank — the side where a void-blade wound from the Nightshelf augur Sivruta~ had left Krath unable to sense approaching threats. This was not tactical preference but compulsion: an obsessive maintenance of formation geometry by a hunter who measured their own worth in usefulness rather than survival.
    
    Maw counted Krath's kills. Including the ones Krath preferred not to acknowledge.
    
    The end came when Krath unwrapped the **Scared Shroud**, a Nightshelf fire-core tome, and channeled its alien fuel through the blood-working **Grulkzul Omega Strike**. Maw identified the danger — fire-knowledge in an engine built for pressure-magic — but held formation rather than confronting Krath. The casting at the Still Pools severed the pod-bond between them and scattered Krath's consciousness across the frozen deep.
    
    Maw survived. A formation of one, drifting the shallows in silence, still counting.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771591661890_0", anchor: "Pods do not reduce to two members through ordinary attrition", text: "Penguin chronicles do not track orca casualties unless celebrating them. Orca oral tradition does not preserve losses unless avenging them. Between these two silences, entire pod histories vanish. I could speculate — encroachment retaliation, inter-pod conflict, a hunt gone wrong — but I would be filling a gap both sides prefer empty.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591661890_1", anchor: "I have not located 'Otrolal in any other record", text: "One summary, one name, zero corroboration. Either 'Otrolal existed and left no mark on the ice or the oral tradition, or someone invented an assailant to give the wound a story. Injuries without authors are harder to carry than injuries with enemies. I understand the impulse. I did not flag it in the main text because I have done the same thing with my own scars.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591661890_2", anchor: "A formation of one, drifting the shallows in silence, still counting", text: "Three ice-impressions from the Still Pools shallows, dated after Krath's dispersal. In each, a single sonar signature traces the same patrol pattern — left-flank coverage for a presence that is not there. The geometry is perfect. The formation is correct. The ice registered this as unremarkable, the way it registers tides and temperature shifts: something that simply continues. The ice is often kinder than it has any right to be.", type: :commentary, display: :full
